    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="d78-01" n="1" xml:id="d78-01"/>

                <head>78. Airgram A–6 From the Department of State to the Embassy in Libya<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d78-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d78-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1971-06-16">June 16, 1971</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Policy Planning Paper</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>REF:</label>
                    <item> CA-5632, November 3, 1970</item>
                </list>
                <p>Attached are three copies of the Policy Planning Paper for Libya, as approved by
                    the members of the NSC Interdepartmental Group for Africa.</p>
                <p>The paper constitutes an official statement of US policy towards Libya and should
                    be used as a guideline by all elements of the Embassy in the preparation of
                    policy statements, action plans and future budgetary projections.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Rogers</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d78-a1.xml" xpointer="d78-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d78-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d78-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, POL 1 LIBYA–US.
                    Secret;Noforn. Covering airgram was drafted by Edward W. Holmes (AF/NSC) and
                    approved by Carter. The annexes are not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d78-f2" n="2" xml:id="d78-f2-content">
                <p>The Department forwarded a Policy Planning Paper for Libya as approved by the NSC
                    Interdepartmental Group for Africa.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
